      "writtenOn": "2022-09-22T16:41:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Major points:\n* Mixing a sync + threaded based approach with an async approach is just going to make the state of things more confusing - pick one rather than doing both. If you\u0027re going to do async, use the async bindings rather than explicitly using handles to a runtime.\n* I don\u0027t think your custom serial poll code is necessary - in general, if you are writing a manual poll implementation, you should really think through whether what you\u0027re doing is necessary.",
      "revId": "eb0828af0c923a1895116b2d6312d3a1af75289a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86511ba5_36dfc899",
        "filename": "uwb/aidl/default/Android.bp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-22T16:41:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please use `liblogger` instead - it\u0027s a wrapper around `env_log` and `android_logger` which can work both on host and device.\n\nIt\u0027s especially relevant in this case, since this HAL is operating off serial and so is theoretically testable on host.",
      "revId": "eb0828af0c923a1895116b2d6312d3a1af75289a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58328701_30fb88e0",
        "filename": "uwb/aidl/default/src/serial.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
