      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-22T16:41:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why can\u0027t you just use a `tokio::fs::File` for the serial port and `.as_raw_fd()` after opening to make the termios calls? This seems like a lot of extra complex code that I\u0027m not seeing a reason for.\n\nThe `new()` operation would be:\nlet file \u003d File::new()\ntermios::stuff(file.as_raw_fd());\n// If you still decide you need separate read/write objects\nlet read_half \u003d file.try_clone();",
      "revId": "eb0828af0c923a1895116b2d6312d3a1af75289a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
